sa<\/jats:italic>-phycobiont which are invaded by the fungal hyphae develop directly into apothecia or pycnidia. The apothecia are thallinocarps. The lichen was collected in the subantarctic Marion Island where it was mainly growing in lichenized tufts of <jats:italic>Scytonema<\/jats:italic>. Two new combinations, <jats:italic>Gonohymenia nigritella<\/jats:italic> (Lettau) Henssen and <jats:italic>G. hondoana<\/jats:italic> (Zahlbr.) Henssen are made.<\/jats:p>","DOI":"10.1017\/s0024282986000063","type":"journal-article","created":{"date-parts":[[2007,5,30]],"date-time":"2007-05-30T06:54:39Z","timestamp":1180508079000},"page":"51-56","source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":4,"title":["<i>EDW Ardiella Mirabilis<\/i>, A Holocarpous Lichen from Marion Island"],"prefix":"10.1017","volume":"18","author":[{"given":"Aino","family":"Henssen","sequence":"first","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]}],"member":"56","published-online":{"date-parts":[[2007,3,28]]},"container-title":["The Lichenologist"],"language":"en","link":[{"URL":"https:\/\/www.cambridge.org\/core\/services\/aop-cambridge-core\/content\/view\/S0024282986000063","content-type":"unspecified","content-version":"vor","intended-application":"similarity-checking"}],"deposited":{"date-parts":[[2019,5,22]],"date-time":"2019-05-22T15:33:34Z","timestamp":1558539214000},"score":26.67189,"resource":{"primary":{"URL":"https:\/\/www.cambridge.org\/core\/product\/identifier\/S0024282986000063\/type\/journal_article"}},"issued":{"date-parts":[[1986,1]]},"references-count":0,"journal-issue":{"issue":"1","published-print":{"date-parts":[[1986,1]]}},"alternative-id":["S0024282986000063"],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1017\/s0024282986000063","ISSN":["0024-2829","1096-1135"],"issn-type":[{"value":"0024-2829","type":"print"},{"value":"1096-1135","type":"electronic"}],"published":{"date-parts":[[1986,1]]}},{"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2022,4,5]],"date-time":"2022-04-05T02:38:56Z","timestamp":1649